Canonical initial migrations for new ERRNO databases only.

This directory is intentionally separate from alembic/versions. The six
existing revisions are retained unchanged because repository history cannot
establish whether another environment has applied them. Do not run the legacy
chain against an empty database; its integer-ID schema does not match the
active FastAPI runtime models.

The canonical environment requires ERRNO_DATABASE_URL and does not load .env.
Non-loopback targets additionally require ERRNO_PGSSLROOTCERT and force
sslmode=verify-full plus ERRNO_ALLOW_CANONICAL_MIGRATION=1. Local migration
validation is limited to the explicitly named errno_phase22_test database with
ERRNO_ALLOW_LOCAL_TEST_DB=1.

Local disposable database example:

    ERRNO_DATABASE_URL='postgresql+psycopg2://postgres@127.0.0.1:55439/errno_phase22_test' \
    ERRNO_ALLOW_LOCAL_TEST_DB=1 \
    .venv/bin/alembic -c alembic_canonical.ini upgrade head

Production command for later review only (not run during Phase 2.2):

    ERRNO_DATABASE_URL="$DATABASE_URL" \
    ERRNO_PGSSLROOTCERT="/absolute/path/to/prod-ca-2021.crt" \
    ERRNO_ALLOW_CANONICAL_MIGRATION=1 \
    .venv/bin/alembic -c alembic_canonical.ini upgrade head
